# 1. ROW_NUMBER()

Assigns a unique number to each row.

## Syntax

```sql
SELECT *,
ROW_NUMBER() OVER(ORDER BY Score DESC) AS RowNumber
FROM Student;
```

### Output

| Name | Score | RowNumber |
|------|------:|----------:|
| Priya |95|1|
| Pooja |95|2|
| Amit |92|3|

---

# ROW_NUMBER() with PARTITION BY

```sql
SELECT *,
ROW_NUMBER() OVER(
PARTITION BY City
ORDER BY Score DESC
) AS RowNumber
FROM Student;
```

---

# 2. RANK()

Assigns the same rank to duplicate values.

```sql
SELECT *,
RANK() OVER(
ORDER BY Score DESC
) AS RankNo
FROM Student;
```

Example

| Score | Rank |
|------:|-----:|
|95|1|
|95|1|
|92|3|

---

# 3. DENSE_RANK()

Assigns the same rank but skips no numbers.

```sql
SELECT *,
DENSE_RANK() OVER(
ORDER BY Score DESC
) AS DenseRank
FROM Student;
```

Example

| Score | Rank |
|------:|-----:|
|95|1|
|95|1|
|92|2|

---

# Difference

| ROW_NUMBER | RANK | DENSE_RANK |
|------------|------|------------|
|Unique Rank|Duplicate Rank|Duplicate Rank|
|No duplicates|Skips ranks|No skipped ranks|

---

# 4. NTILE()

Divides rows into equal groups.

```sql
SELECT *,
NTILE(4) OVER(
ORDER BY Score DESC
) AS Quartile
FROM Student;
```

---

# 5. LAG()

Returns previous row value.

```sql
SELECT *,
LAG(Score) OVER(
ORDER BY Score
) AS PreviousScore
FROM Student;
```

---

# 6. LEAD()

Returns next row value.

```sql
SELECT *,
LEAD(Score) OVER(
ORDER BY Score
) AS NextScore
FROM Student;
```

---

# Difference

| LAG() | LEAD() |
|--------|---------|
|Previous Row|Next Row|

---

# 7. FIRST_VALUE()

Returns first value in the window.

```sql
SELECT *,
FIRST_VALUE(Score)
OVER(
ORDER BY Score DESC
) AS HighestScore
FROM Student;
```

---

# 8. LAST_VALUE()

Returns last value in the window.

```sql
SELECT *,
LAST_VALUE(Score)
OVER(
ORDER BY Score DESC
ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING
AND UNBOUNDED FOLLOWING
) AS LowestScore
FROM Student;
```

