# Most Asked Interview Questions

## Q1. What is a Window Function?

A window function performs calculations across related rows without grouping the rows into a single result.

---

## Q2. Difference between GROUP BY and Window Function?

| GROUP BY | Window Function |
|-----------|-----------------|
|Returns one row per group|Returns every row|
|Uses Aggregate Functions|Uses OVER()|
|Reduces rows|Does not reduce rows|

---

## Q3. What is OVER()?

OVER() defines the window on which the function operates.

---

## Q4. Difference between ROW_NUMBER(), RANK(), and DENSE_RANK()?

| Function | Duplicate Rank | Skips Rank |
|-----------|----------------|------------|
|ROW_NUMBER|No|No|
|RANK|Yes|Yes|
|DENSE_RANK|Yes|No|

---

## Q5. Difference between LAG() and LEAD()?

| LAG() | LEAD() |
|--------|---------|
|Previous row|Next row|

---

## Q6. Why is PARTITION BY used?

It divides data into logical groups while keeping all rows in the result.

---

## Q7. Can Aggregate Functions be used as Window Functions?

Yes.

- SUM()
- AVG()
- COUNT()
- MAX()
- MIN()

